        "node_id": "n_5_46b736",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: To ensure that we find the correct dimensions \\( m \\) and \\( k \\), we need to iterate through possible values of \\( k \\) more efficiently and ensure that we do not prematurely conclude that no solution exists. Instead of returning \"impossible\" immediately upon finding no valid pair, we should continue iterating until all possible values of \\( k \\) have been checked. This will allow us to find the correct dimensions if they exist within the given constraints.",
